{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdZ39GLnqaxMEzentZcC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Zest, a restaurant discovery app, has moved its recommendations into a text thread. On Thursday the startup launched a restaurant concierge that users message directly. It can check availability and book a table through OpenTable, Resy and SevenRooms. It can also be added to a group chat, where it blends everyone's tastes, runs an in-thread vote when people can't decide, and books for the group without anyone leaving the conversation.\n\nWhat separates it from a general-purpose assistant is where its knowledge of you comes from. Zest links to users' credit cards through Plaid and looks only at food and drink transactions, so it starts from places you have actually eaten instead of a questionnaire. CEO Mario Gomez-Hall says this lets it learn a person's taste faster than a general assistant. That is his claim, and the article offers no comparison that tests it. TechCrunch's own tests found that the AI worked fairly well, suggesting new places that fit their tastes and conditions like time of day, party size and location. TechCrunch also noted that finding an open table is something other apps have offered for years, and that the added value is the convenience of texting back and forth about options and getting available times in the same conversation.\n\nThe revenue plan explains why the format matters to the company. Zest has thousands of users and hopes the move to text helps it scale and generate revenue. Gomez-Hall calls booking and ordering the first revenue lines, with food ordering still to come, and he says there are transactions to participate in. The article gives no figures on how much those transactions might earn, so whether a concierge that books tables can support a business remains unproven. The company is also considering extending beyond restaurants to businesses and shopping, but that is only a possibility at this stage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2766,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2766},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f6f2469-b340-40e3-afd3-e0991fea34a9","uuid":"81e0d36f-b0f0-4133-9982-d5276c792336","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:31:32.890Z","request_id":"req_011CgdZ395C6jBTTvfqrJQ6F"}
